WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.174
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.175 --> 00:02.467
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION, BINGE
DRINKING, SHAMEFUL ACTS NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:02.468 --> 00:03.760
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:03.761 --> 00:04.969
DUE TO RECENT COMPLIANCE ISSUES, THE
BLACK DOT SIZE HAS BEEN INCREASED BY 5%.

00:04.970 --> 00:06.305
Seriously.

00:06.514 --> 00:08.516
What an idiot.

00:09.517 --> 00:11.852
The fact that you have a crush on him...

00:12.228 --> 00:14.271
is painfully obvious even to me.

00:26.116 --> 00:28.576
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

00:28.577 --> 00:31.788
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3To a city far away, what do you say?

00:31.789 --> 00:34.207
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

00:34.208 --> 00:37.753
To a city far away, what do you say?

00:41.840 --> 00:43.716
Wait a sec, another heatwave?

00:43.717 --> 00:45.426
Temperatures are rising... Huh?!

00:45.427 --> 00:48.638
Our original plans are
totally busted, what now?

00:48.639 --> 00:51.474
But honestly, I'm getting so hyped

00:51.475 --> 00:54.143
Alright, let's roll up
our sleeves and dive in

00:54.144 --> 00:55.895
Rub your sleepy eyes and jump up

00:55.896 --> 00:57.355
Grab the usual shades

00:57.356 --> 01:00.275
Check your gear: Iced coffee, thermos

01:00.276 --> 01:02.944
Clear blue skies, just a trick of summer

01:02.945 --> 01:06.073
The booming speakers
keep calling my name

01:06.407 --> 01:08.909
Even now, I still believe

01:11.829 --> 01:13.788
In unexpected encounters

01:13.789 --> 01:16.374
And the miracles of this season

01:16.375 --> 01:19.627
Summer brings
those swing swing emotions

01:19.628 --> 01:22.380
Ah, even if I get a little carried away

01:22.381 --> 01:27.594
On my mind,
I've only been searching for you

01:27.595 --> 01:33.516
Let the south wind blow you here,
just as you are

01:33.517 --> 01:38.230
Under the blue sky, hold me tight

01:39.064 --> 01:44.486
I want to dream
a summer dream with you

01:50.409 --> 01:53.704
I didn't expect Kouhei to figure it out.

01:54.705 --> 01:57.166
Could it be... you feel
that way about Kitahara?

01:57.708 --> 02:01.503
But he still isn't certain.

02:03.172 --> 02:06.258
I have to play dumb it till the end!

02:07.134 --> 02:08.384
Good morning.

02:08.385 --> 02:09.594
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

02:09.595 --> 02:10.471
Good morning.

02:11.096 --> 02:13.932
Today's breakfast is
my and Chisa's turn, right?

02:14.308 --> 02:16.267
Yeah, what should we make?

02:16.268 --> 02:18.311
We still have canned Spam, so...

02:18.312 --> 02:19.562
Hold on, Kitahara.

02:19.563 --> 02:20.439
Huh?

02:20.564 --> 02:23.025
Switch breakfast duty with me today.

02:23.400 --> 02:24.902
Why the sudden change?

02:25.319 --> 02:26.986
I'm just in the mood for it.

02:26.987 --> 02:28.280
Let's go, Kotegawa.

02:32.660 --> 02:33.494
Wink.

02:35.537 --> 02:36.580
What the hell?

02:38.999 --> 02:42.585
This morning's tasks include
carrying equipment, updating the blog,

02:42.586 --> 02:43.836
and sorting receipts?

02:43.837 --> 02:46.005
Who's doing what?

02:46.006 --> 02:48.925
Doing the blog and receipts
means staying in the cool room.

02:48.926 --> 02:50.593
Let's play Rock-Paper-Stripper for it.

02:50.594 --> 02:52.721
I'll take the equipment carrying duty.

02:53.263 --> 02:54.098
Huh?

02:54.556 --> 02:55.973
It's really hot outside.

02:55.974 --> 02:59.061
It's fine.
I'm in the mood to enjoy the heat.

02:59.937 --> 03:01.145
Oh, right.

03:01.146 --> 03:03.315
I'm going to focus on work,

03:03.732 --> 03:07.193
so I absolutely will not step inside
for the next two hours.

03:07.194 --> 03:08.237
Wink.

03:09.321 --> 03:11.407
Does that guy have a fever or something?

03:16.870 --> 03:19.330
Can you pour me a cup of tea, Cakey?

03:19.331 --> 03:20.290
Ah, sure.

03:20.582 --> 03:21.458
Here you go.

03:22.459 --> 03:23.293
Thanks.

03:24.670 --> 03:26.879
You two are so close.

03:26.880 --> 03:28.131
Where did that come from?

03:28.132 --> 03:31.718
That exchange just now seemed like
a married couple of ten years.

03:31.719 --> 03:34.096
She just poured me a cup of tea.

03:34.304 --> 03:36.306
Maybe you two should...

03:36.598 --> 03:39.101
try dating each other?

03:39.309 --> 03:40.811
Such horrible wingman!

03:41.937 --> 03:42.895
What are you doing?

03:42.896 --> 03:44.522
I should be asking you that!

03:44.523 --> 03:46.650
What's with all your antics since morning?

03:47.109 --> 03:49.736
What do you mean?
It's exactly as it looks.

03:49.737 --> 03:52.238
I see. Deliberately trying
to annoy me, huh?

03:52.239 --> 03:53.407
How did it come to that?

03:53.532 --> 03:54.824
Hypothetically speaking!

03:54.825 --> 03:57.369
Just a "what if"!
Even though it's impossible!

03:57.578 --> 03:59.913
If I happened to have someone I liked,

04:00.122 --> 04:03.834
those unnatural actions would
actually make things awkward for me!

04:06.920 --> 04:08.005
Understood?

04:08.756 --> 04:09.882
Got it.

04:10.132 --> 04:11.674
You're a tsundere, right?

04:11.675 --> 04:13.927
Someone throw this guy
on a mountain, please!

04:14.303 --> 04:17.347
What should I do? I denied it so fiercely.

04:18.223 --> 04:21.685
What you asked yesterday
was really just a misunderstanding.

04:21.935 --> 04:22.727
No.

04:22.728 --> 04:26.481
Maybe because I overreacted in
denying it, he became suspicious?

04:26.482 --> 04:29.777
If I just ignore it, he'll probably
lose interest eventually.

04:31.236 --> 04:32.863
Do whatever you want.

04:33.197 --> 04:34.198
Understood.

04:35.824 --> 04:38.242
Leave everything to me, wink.

04:38.243 --> 04:39.870
Not a chance in hell.

04:41.955 --> 04:43.123
Hey, Kitahara.

04:43.373 --> 04:44.458
What?

04:44.666 --> 04:46.376
Do you like love fortune-telling?

04:46.752 --> 04:47.377
Huh?

04:48.462 --> 04:50.881
Why are you asking
such a weirdly cheesy question?

04:51.006 --> 04:54.509
Oh, so you like it that much?
You shy, innocent boy.

04:54.510 --> 04:56.053
Listen to me!

04:56.303 --> 04:59.389
Then let me tell your fortune.

05:00.057 --> 05:01.891
Whatever, do what you want.

05:01.892 --> 05:04.228
Draw a card.

05:04.353 --> 05:05.062
Oh.

05:06.313 --> 05:07.564
What did you get?

05:07.815 --> 05:09.191
3 of Diamonds.

05:09.399 --> 05:11.317
Okay, I understand everything now.

05:11.318 --> 05:14.029
You understand everything
from just drawing one card?

05:14.238 --> 05:16.573
Since you drew
the 3 of Diamonds, you'll...

05:17.199 --> 05:21.077
end up with a girl around your age
who lives nearby, born in the countryside,

05:21.078 --> 05:23.871
wears extremely flashy makeup,
and constantly dreams of

05:23.872 --> 05:25.206
a romance like in a TV drama.

05:25.207 --> 05:26.959
That's way too specific!

05:28.752 --> 05:30.545
Knock it off with the fortune-telling!

05:30.546 --> 05:31.505
Understood.

05:33.507 --> 05:34.758
Hey, Kitahara.

05:35.133 --> 05:36.260
What is it now?

05:36.718 --> 05:38.594
Do you want to do a psychological test?

05:38.595 --> 05:39.220
Huh?

05:39.221 --> 05:40.639
H-He's pulling another trick.

05:40.889 --> 05:42.766
What scheme are you plotting?

05:42.933 --> 05:45.560
I just want to know your true feelings.

05:45.561 --> 05:47.144
Stop it. It's disgusting.

05:47.145 --> 05:48.688
Alright, let's begin.

05:48.689 --> 05:49.857
Seriously.

05:50.023 --> 05:51.692
He says that but plays along anyway.

05:52.192 --> 05:56.196
You're invited to a party hosted by
an important figure in your company.

05:56.446 --> 05:58.155
Among the luxurious dishes,

05:58.156 --> 06:00.867
there is one dish
that you absolutely detest.

06:00.868 --> 06:04.329
The question is,
what would you do in that situation?

06:04.705 --> 06:05.706
Hmm.

06:05.914 --> 06:07.791
A dish I detest?

06:07.916 --> 06:08.917
What about you, Cakey?

06:09.084 --> 06:10.627
Eh, me too?

06:10.794 --> 06:14.046
If it were me, I'd probably just
force myself to eat it all.

06:14.047 --> 06:15.132
I see.

06:15.340 --> 06:19.428
Apparently, this question reveals
what kind of person is suitable for you.

06:19.761 --> 06:20.137
Huh?

06:20.554 --> 06:23.347
Someone who's fun-loving and
is surprisingly adaptable

06:23.348 --> 06:24.682
is your perfect match.

06:24.683 --> 06:25.308
Wink.

06:25.309 --> 06:26.560
Oh...

06:27.019 --> 06:28.769
Then, what about you?

06:28.770 --> 06:30.397
Actually...

06:30.564 --> 06:33.983
because there's no food I hate,
I can't imagine it at all.

06:33.984 --> 06:37.528
So this test doesn't really apply to me.

06:37.529 --> 06:39.907
I see. In other words,

06:40.115 --> 06:42.158
for someone like you
who doesn't hate anything,

06:42.159 --> 06:45.579
a partner with a weird face
and heavy makeup is the best match!

06:47.039 --> 06:49.206
What if I honestly said I couldn't eat it?

06:49.207 --> 06:50.625
For an honest person like you,

06:50.626 --> 06:53.419
a partner with a weird face and
heavy makeup would be a great match!

06:53.420 --> 06:55.212
Try a bit, and leave it if it's no good...

06:55.213 --> 06:57.256
For a brave soul
who tries anything like you,

06:57.257 --> 07:00.217
a partner with a weird face
and heavy makeup is the best!

07:00.218 --> 07:01.469
Deliberately spill it then...

07:01.470 --> 07:02.846
For a quick-witted person like you...

07:03.263 --> 07:04.722
Kouhei, let's step outside.

07:04.723 --> 07:05.390
Roger.

07:05.557 --> 07:06.224
Huh?

07:06.934 --> 07:08.769
That's enough!

07:09.102 --> 07:11.188
You said to do whatever I want.

07:11.438 --> 07:14.107
This clueless, well-meaning idiocy
is the absolute worst!

07:14.566 --> 07:15.858
Listen to me.

07:15.859 --> 07:16.776
What is it?

07:16.777 --> 07:19.196
Hypothetically! Just hypothetically!

07:19.446 --> 07:20.655
Let's say I...

07:20.656 --> 07:21.656
(actually have)

07:21.657 --> 07:24.075
f-f-f-f-feelings for Iori.

07:24.076 --> 07:24.743
Yeah.

07:25.243 --> 07:28.246
Then why are you putting
so much effort into helping me?

07:29.164 --> 07:31.959
You don't get any benefit from it.

07:36.630 --> 07:37.589
Kouhei?

07:38.256 --> 07:39.882
Honestly, that's a good question.

07:39.883 --> 07:40.967
Huh?

07:40.968 --> 07:42.886
Now that you mention it, you're right.

07:43.178 --> 07:45.639
Why am I doing something
that brings me no benefit?

07:45.847 --> 07:49.059
What? You don't even
understand it yourself?

07:49.351 --> 07:51.186
Well, if I had to say...

07:51.561 --> 07:54.523
maybe it's because I understand
that feeling that's so strong,

07:54.773 --> 07:56.525
it can't be suppressed.

08:01.697 --> 08:03.073
So that means...

08:03.365 --> 08:05.450
you also have someone you like?

08:05.659 --> 08:08.078
Ah, I haven't told you yet.

08:08.370 --> 08:12.123
I used to be an otaku
with an incredibly passionate love...

08:12.124 --> 08:14.166
Ah, yeah, got it.

08:14.167 --> 08:16.169
That's why I'll help you.

08:17.879 --> 08:21.215
Leaving him to do his weird antics
would be a pain too.

08:21.216 --> 08:24.094
I guess I'll just
keep him in check for now.

08:25.095 --> 08:27.972
Then try asking a roundabout question.

08:27.973 --> 08:29.766
Hmm, what should I ask?

08:32.310 --> 08:34.896
What scheme are those two plotting?

08:41.319 --> 08:43.529
Hello, this is Dolphin.

08:43.530 --> 08:44.531
Hello?

08:44.948 --> 08:48.034
This is Sugita
calling from World Wide Tours.

08:48.035 --> 08:48.493
Yes.

08:48.660 --> 08:50.703
Is Kotegawa-sama available?

08:50.704 --> 08:52.789
Yes, please hold for a moment.

08:53.290 --> 08:54.791
Auntie, phone call for you.

08:54.958 --> 08:56.710
Auntie, phone call!

09:02.758 --> 09:03.799
Boss!

09:03.800 --> 09:04.593
Huh?

09:04.801 --> 09:05.926
What's wrong?

09:05.927 --> 09:06.970
A phone call for you.

09:08.972 --> 09:09.555
Yes.

09:09.556 --> 09:11.683
So she don't like being called Auntie?

09:11.975 --> 09:13.351
Hey, Kitahara.

09:13.643 --> 09:14.603
You again.

09:15.187 --> 09:16.313
What is it this time?

09:16.480 --> 09:18.273
I have a question for you.

09:19.357 --> 09:22.777
Just ask whether he sees me
as someone of the opposite sex.

09:22.778 --> 09:25.197
Understood. I'll try asking it
in a roundabout way.

09:25.947 --> 09:27.115
Do you...

09:31.328 --> 09:32.788
want to "do it" with Cakey?

09:34.790 --> 09:36.957
Ah! Ouch! That hurt!

09:36.958 --> 09:39.835
What the hell is he trying to do?

09:39.836 --> 09:42.005
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3

09:42.380 --> 09:44.216
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work, everyone.

09:44.925 --> 09:46.676
You guys can really drink.

09:47.969 --> 09:50.054
Aina-chan, thank you for today.

09:50.055 --> 09:51.723
No, it's my pleasure.

09:52.057 --> 09:54.351
Thanks for the BBQ.

09:54.601 --> 09:56.937
Let's drink again
when we get back to Japan.

09:57.062 --> 09:58.605
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work, everyone.

09:59.564 --> 10:02.651
The customers
seem to really like you, Aina.

10:03.193 --> 10:06.196
You drank quite a bit too,
are you okay?

10:06.655 --> 10:08.323
Yes, I'm fine with this much.

10:08.740 --> 10:11.827
Then we'll go clean up the grill.

10:11.952 --> 10:13.203
I'm counting on you guys.

10:13.662 --> 10:16.455
They seem to have
gotten used to the work too.

10:16.456 --> 10:17.456
That's right.

10:17.457 --> 10:20.334
It's been ten days
since they arrived, hasn't it?

10:20.335 --> 10:22.087
I guess it's been about that long.

10:23.088 --> 10:25.841
Men and women living together
for ten days, huh?

10:26.424 --> 10:29.511
I wonder how those two are
taking care of that business?

10:29.886 --> 10:31.429
Give it a rest.

10:32.139 --> 10:32.930
I mean,

10:32.931 --> 10:36.726
if a guy doesn't "release" it
for two weeks, he'll die, right?

10:36.893 --> 10:38.102
Right, right.

10:38.103 --> 10:40.354
That place will burst
and they'll die, right?

10:40.355 --> 10:43.358
Since they're together 24/7,
how can they possibly take care of it?

10:43.567 --> 10:46.111
That's true.
Young people really have it rough.

10:46.987 --> 10:48.113
Seriously?

10:50.407 --> 10:52.993
The manager told me about
what happened earlier today.

10:53.577 --> 10:56.328
I heard you noticed
a male customer's strap was loose,

10:56.329 --> 10:57.747
so you helped him retie it.

10:58.206 --> 10:58.831
And...

10:58.832 --> 11:01.668
at that time, you accidentally
pinched his "you know what," right?

11:02.460 --> 11:04.087
Because I wasn't paying attention.

11:04.254 --> 11:06.255
But I didn't tighten it that hard.

11:06.256 --> 11:09.217
They don't call it a man's
weak spot for nothing.

11:09.593 --> 11:10.427
Seriously.

11:10.719 --> 11:13.346
Why are you so clumsy?

11:13.805 --> 11:14.806
I'm sorry.

11:15.974 --> 11:20.395
Nanaka isn't familiar with those things,
but she's surprisingly good at them.

11:21.021 --> 11:24.607
Well, time to learn a thing or two
about the sexes

11:24.608 --> 11:26.276
that you didn't get from health class.

11:31.865 --> 11:33.617
Chisa! Chisa!

11:34.034 --> 11:35.159
What's wrong?

11:35.160 --> 11:37.454
It might be an emergency.

11:37.787 --> 11:39.371
Another problem with the customers?

11:39.372 --> 11:40.373
Ah, no.

11:40.498 --> 11:41.666
It's not that.

11:41.791 --> 11:43.792
Iori and Kouhei are going to die.

11:43.793 --> 11:45.837
We just saw the customers off,
what happened?

11:46.421 --> 11:48.297
Or were they in a traffic accident?

11:48.298 --> 11:50.258
No, that's not it.

11:50.467 --> 11:52.593
"That place" will burst and they'll die!

11:52.594 --> 11:54.262
That's beyond my imagination!

11:54.387 --> 11:56.431
Tell me the details.

11:56.556 --> 11:58.933
WHISPER
I'm not too familiar with guys,

11:58.934 --> 12:00.477
WHISPER
so I'm not entirely sure either.

12:00.936 --> 12:02.103
You see, for guys...

12:03.021 --> 12:05.522
if they don't "release" it
for two weeks, they'll die.

12:05.523 --> 12:06.066
Huh?

12:06.441 --> 12:07.775
Such a ridiculous myth...

12:07.776 --> 12:09.527
I also thought it was impossible.

12:09.778 --> 12:11.070
But, but,

12:11.071 --> 12:13.572
just think back to their daily actions.

12:13.573 --> 12:15.074
Daily actions?

12:15.075 --> 12:15.366
THE SECRET WHISPERS OF THE SECRETARY - JOTAKANO AYANO

12:15.367 --> 12:16.450
THE SECRET WHISPERS OF THE SECRETARY - JOTAKANO AYANO
UNUSUAL OBSESSION WITH PORN You know, the things

12:16.451 --> 12:18.535
THE SECRET WHISPERS OF THE SECRETARY - JOTAKANO AYANO
UNUSUAL OBSESSION WITH PORN that us girls can never understand.

12:18.536 --> 12:18.953
UNUSUAL OBSESSION WITH PORN that us girls can never understand.

12:18.954 --> 12:21.039
DANGEROUS LOOK WHEN
LOOKING AT THE OPPOSITE SEX

12:21.998 --> 12:23.458
Now that you mention it.

12:24.042 --> 12:27.379
I always thought they were just emotions
I completely couldn't comprehend.

12:27.629 --> 12:28.964
But if everything...

12:29.714 --> 12:31.674
was a matter of life and death...

12:31.675 --> 12:33.176
Then it all makes sense, right?

12:33.551 --> 12:36.513
No, but that didn't happen
when we went to Okinawa.

12:36.680 --> 12:38.847
We only stayed there for five nights.

12:38.848 --> 12:41.017
Besides, when Iori got weak back then...

12:41.601 --> 12:43.603
I invited Iori to do it.

12:45.063 --> 12:47.523
I think that was a medical procedure.

12:47.524 --> 12:49.234
Is that how it is?!

12:49.609 --> 12:51.986
But I've never heard of
such a cause of death.

12:51.987 --> 12:53.321
That's true.

12:53.822 --> 12:56.700
But maybe it's just that
we don't know about it?

12:57.867 --> 13:01.412
Well, time to learn a thing or two
about the sexes

13:01.413 --> 13:03.123
that you didn't get from health class.

13:04.833 --> 13:06.668
Then let's just confirm it.

13:06.793 --> 13:07.752
Confirm what?

13:08.461 --> 13:10.130
Iori and Kouhei's condition.

13:12.966 --> 13:14.508
Good job, you two.

13:14.509 --> 13:15.719
Are you done cleaning up?

13:17.637 --> 13:19.138
Are you okay, Kouhei?

13:19.139 --> 13:20.348
Does it hurt a lot?

13:20.932 --> 13:24.018
Sorry, could you rub my back?

13:24.019 --> 13:24.644
Yeah.

13:25.020 --> 13:27.480
Don't push yourself too hard.

13:29.524 --> 13:31.609
It turned out to be true!

13:32.193 --> 13:33.485
I can't believe it.

13:33.486 --> 13:37.490
But Iori is actually worried
about Kouhei so seriously.

13:37.824 --> 13:40.367
NORMAL
Normally, he'd just point and laugh.

13:40.368 --> 13:41.369
NORMAL
That's true.

13:41.953 --> 13:44.873
The male body is really troublesome.

13:44.998 --> 13:46.833
Yeah, I had no idea.

13:47.250 --> 13:51.003
But, didn't they anticipate
this situation beforehand?

13:51.004 --> 13:53.757
Yeah, making absolutely
no preparations...

13:53.923 --> 13:55.383
- Ah.
- What's wrong?

13:55.717 --> 13:58.011
I think they did prepare.

14:01.598 --> 14:02.806
No way.

14:02.807 --> 14:04.683
It was confiscated?

14:04.684 --> 14:07.270
Because that's not something
you can just take outside.

14:07.520 --> 14:10.522
The time until it bursts
is two weeks, right?

14:10.523 --> 14:12.442
Yeah, that's what I heard.

14:13.026 --> 14:14.903
Then...

14:17.489 --> 14:19.783
There are only... three days left.

14:23.536 --> 14:25.038
Are you okay now?

14:26.247 --> 14:28.083
Yeah. More or less.

14:28.416 --> 14:30.876
I completely understand your pain.

14:30.877 --> 14:33.630
Who would've thought
they'd put a pole there.

14:35.840 --> 14:38.801
But today's work is pretty much over.

14:38.802 --> 14:41.179
Let's enjoy a fun time
drinking some beer!

14:47.477 --> 14:48.520
What's going on?

14:48.895 --> 14:51.980
Why are they looking at us
with such pity in their eyes?

14:51.981 --> 14:52.815
Almost like...

14:52.816 --> 14:55.777
"How pitiful, but he's going to
die tomorrow anyway."

14:56.486 --> 14:57.404
Iori...

14:58.154 --> 14:59.197
Kouhei...

15:00.031 --> 15:01.657
- Thanks for everything up to now.
- Thanks for everything up to now.

15:01.658 --> 15:02.908
- Hey!
- Hey!

15:02.909 --> 15:04.660
Why the sudden thanks?

15:04.661 --> 15:06.371
Did something happen?

15:06.579 --> 15:07.789
Don't worry about it.

15:08.164 --> 15:10.208
We can't be of any help anyway.

15:10.625 --> 15:13.836
We just want to say thank you
because you two are still alive.

15:13.837 --> 15:14.753
Truly, thank you.

15:14.754 --> 15:16.047
Are you trying to be a rapper?!

15:17.257 --> 15:19.801
You two want to drink beer, right?

15:19.968 --> 15:21.719
If you don't mind, it's my treat.

15:21.886 --> 15:24.848
We'll take care of
the rest of the cleaning.

15:25.014 --> 15:27.350
You two go ahead and drink.

15:27.475 --> 15:29.227
- Ah, okay...
- Ah, okay...

15:32.105 --> 15:33.856
Something is definitely wrong.

15:33.857 --> 15:34.524
Yeah.

15:34.691 --> 15:37.192
Even if I try to think of
a reason they'd be mad...

15:37.193 --> 15:39.612
They've never looked at us
with those eyes before.

15:40.321 --> 15:43.365
Moreover, they were looking at
our lower halves just now.

15:43.366 --> 15:44.617
Our lower halves?

15:45.201 --> 15:45.994
Yeah.

15:46.411 --> 15:47.495
What's the matter?

15:47.787 --> 15:48.788
Lower halves...

15:49.289 --> 15:50.498
Pitying eyes...

15:50.999 --> 15:52.125
Foreigners...

15:52.625 --> 15:54.126
Huh! Don't tell me...

15:54.127 --> 15:56.254
Ah, you realized it too?

15:56.588 --> 16:00.048
They might be comparing
our sizes with the locals.

16:00.049 --> 16:00.967
Damn it!

16:01.509 --> 16:03.385
But is that really it?

16:03.386 --> 16:05.180
Even though
we don't have concrete proof,

16:05.513 --> 16:07.181
then let's just empirically prove it.

16:07.182 --> 16:08.141
Empirically prove it?

16:08.349 --> 16:10.559
When Cakey got drunk and stripped,

16:10.560 --> 16:14.814
try imagining her sandwiched between
Azusa-san and Nanaka-san.

16:20.403 --> 16:22.697
Yes, that's the exact same look!

16:23.156 --> 16:26.283
The exact same look
when comparing sizes?

16:26.284 --> 16:29.203
I'm 90% sure that deduction is spot on.

16:29.204 --> 16:30.205
God damn it!

16:30.413 --> 16:32.247
Why is reality so cruel?

16:32.248 --> 16:34.834
Yeah, the 3D world is truly garbage!

16:35.251 --> 16:37.879
But if that's the case,
there's nothing we can do about it.

16:38.046 --> 16:39.796
The competition here is just too stiff.

16:39.797 --> 16:41.715
Even if that look has a bit of pity...

16:41.716 --> 16:44.218
If swallowing our pride means
accepting their sympathy,

16:44.219 --> 16:45.886
then I say we let them buy us free beer.

16:45.887 --> 16:47.680
I can live with that.

16:50.475 --> 16:51.518
So...

16:51.809 --> 16:54.061
what should we do?

16:54.062 --> 16:56.481
Of course,
the best thing to do is obviously...

16:59.067 --> 16:59.984
Impossible.

17:00.735 --> 17:01.611
I guess so.

17:01.819 --> 17:03.696
Is there any other way?

17:08.117 --> 17:08.951
PaB FRESHMEN

17:08.952 --> 17:12.539
We have some urgent business so we
definitely won't be home for two hours.

17:12.872 --> 17:13.748
Do your best!

17:14.916 --> 17:16.792
- What's the meaning of this?
- What's the meaning of this?

17:16.793 --> 17:17.918
Is this okay?

17:17.919 --> 17:18.544
Yeah.

17:18.545 --> 17:20.880
It should be fine.
Though I don't really get it.

17:22.173 --> 17:22.757
Huh?

17:22.924 --> 17:24.925
You two are still here?

17:24.926 --> 17:27.136
Boss and Chief have already left.

17:27.470 --> 17:28.388
Maki-san.

17:28.638 --> 17:30.472
Well, something came up...

17:30.473 --> 17:33.725
We're just planning to kill
about two hours here.

17:33.726 --> 17:34.686
Oh...

17:34.894 --> 17:37.188
Then I'll give the shop keys to you two.

17:37.480 --> 17:38.856
Thank you.

17:40.316 --> 17:43.026
Make sure you don't forget it
at the dorm tomorrow.

17:43.027 --> 17:44.070
- Okay.
- Okay.

17:46.990 --> 17:49.533
Anyway, why specifically two hours?

17:49.534 --> 17:51.369
Ah, about that, um...

17:51.536 --> 17:53.079
It's a physiological matter...

17:53.746 --> 17:56.249
regarding Iori and Kouhei.

17:56.416 --> 17:57.083
Huh?

17:57.709 --> 17:57.916
LOVE HOTEL - REST 2H: 4,500 YEN The signs often say "Short Stay: 2 Hours."

17:57.917 --> 18:00.627
LOVE HOTEL - REST 2H: 4,500 YEN The signs often say "Short Stay: 2 Hours."
A LIFELINE ONCE EVERY TWO WEEKS OVERNIGHT, 10 PM - 12 PM: 7,000 YEN

18:00.628 --> 18:00.794
A LIFELINE ONCE EVERY TWO WEEKS OVERNIGHT, 10 PM - 12 PM: 7,000 YEN

18:00.795 --> 18:02.796
Huh? Don't tell me those two...

18:02.797 --> 18:03.464
Heh?

18:03.673 --> 18:05.215
That's how it is.

18:05.216 --> 18:08.428
So we're planning to go
kill some time before returning.

18:08.595 --> 18:10.470
I-I see...

18:10.471 --> 18:11.806
Those two?

18:12.140 --> 18:13.682
Thanks for your hard work.

18:13.683 --> 18:14.809
Thank you.

18:17.562 --> 18:19.563
We still have an hour left.

18:19.564 --> 18:20.940
What should we do?

18:21.399 --> 18:21.648
DIVING DOCUMENTARY ENDLESS BLUE

18:21.649 --> 18:23.650
DIVING DOCUMENTARY ENDLESS BLUE
BLUE WORLD 2 How about watching a diving DVD?

18:23.651 --> 18:23.900
DIVING DOCUMENTARY ENDLESS BLUE

18:23.901 --> 18:26.945
DIVING DOCUMENTARY ENDLESS BLUE
We just saw it with our own eyes, so watching a DVD is a bit...

18:26.946 --> 18:27.195
DIVING DOCUMENTARY ENDLESS BLUE

18:27.196 --> 18:29.866
But I like watching DVDs too.

18:30.325 --> 18:33.494
All you ever think about
is diving, isn't it?

18:33.828 --> 18:34.787
Is that so?

18:34.996 --> 18:35.997
It really is.

18:37.665 --> 18:39.250
I'm a little jealous.

18:42.253 --> 18:43.296
Jealous of what?

18:43.504 --> 18:46.883
Because you have something
that you're so passionate about.

18:47.133 --> 18:48.801
Is that how it is?

18:49.177 --> 18:50.261
Yeah.

18:51.179 --> 18:53.640
I'm truly jealous.

18:54.265 --> 18:56.892
People who are passionate
about something

18:56.893 --> 18:58.478
look really cool, don't they?

19:01.147 --> 19:03.775
You want to become a diving
instructor in the future, right?

19:03.900 --> 19:04.609
Yeah.

19:04.817 --> 19:07.403
Then why did you enroll in engineering?

19:10.615 --> 19:11.366
Chisa?

19:11.658 --> 19:14.535
Ah, sorry. I guess
I shouldn't have asked that.

19:14.786 --> 19:16.245
Ah, it's fine.

19:16.954 --> 19:19.791
I was originally good at
science subjects anyway.

19:20.333 --> 19:21.334
And also...

19:21.751 --> 19:24.253
I had a little argument with my mom.

19:24.587 --> 19:26.172
It's like a trade-off condition.

19:26.506 --> 19:27.548
I see.

19:28.132 --> 19:31.469
It seems my mom doesn't want
me to be a diving instructor.

19:32.428 --> 19:33.471
I see.

19:37.517 --> 19:41.145
I... want to be my older sister.

19:41.521 --> 19:43.981
You mean you wish you were born first?

19:44.482 --> 19:45.900
That's not wrong either.

19:46.484 --> 19:47.984
She's good at communicating.

19:47.985 --> 19:49.487
Always smiling.

19:49.696 --> 19:50.947
Loves the sea very much.

19:51.239 --> 19:53.407
Despite how she looks,
she's good at her job.

19:53.408 --> 19:57.245
I was just thinking how much better
it would've been if I were her.

19:59.497 --> 20:02.166
The feeling of
wanting to be someone else?

20:03.126 --> 20:04.419
I know that saying this...

20:06.838 --> 20:09.590
will make me look very pathetic.

20:13.094 --> 20:15.805
I want... to be you.

20:16.556 --> 20:17.432
Me?

20:18.474 --> 20:20.727
Ah um, what I meant just now was...

20:20.852 --> 20:22.895
I want to be you too.

20:23.062 --> 20:23.521
Huh?

20:24.272 --> 20:26.773
Becoming someone like me
won't get you anything.

20:26.774 --> 20:29.986
You were so friendly
with the customers today.

20:30.653 --> 20:33.448
I don't have a talent for that.

20:34.615 --> 20:35.491
Chisa.

20:39.036 --> 20:41.414
Talking about this
won't solve anything, will it?

20:41.748 --> 20:44.125
Yeah, just chasing pipedreams.

20:44.417 --> 20:47.044
In the end, I am still just me.

20:47.712 --> 20:50.798
- You two look like you're having fun.
- You two look like you're having fun.

20:54.177 --> 20:56.678
I-Iori and Imamura-kun?

20:56.679 --> 20:58.347
What are you so mad about?

20:58.598 --> 21:00.724
Are you freaking kidding me?

21:00.725 --> 21:04.103
Maki-san was skulking around
just now, and...

21:04.687 --> 21:07.440
What the hell do you mean
we are an item!?

21:07.815 --> 21:09.149
What are you talking about?

21:09.150 --> 21:12.194
We just wanted to give you guys
the time and space to...

21:12.195 --> 21:14.446
Time and space to
do what with this guy!?

21:14.447 --> 21:16.616
Even as a prank, there's a limit!

21:18.159 --> 21:19.160
So basically...

21:19.410 --> 21:22.288
the thing between Iori and Kouhei
was just a misunderstanding.

21:23.206 --> 21:24.664
I see.

21:24.665 --> 21:26.292
I should be the one apologizing.

21:26.501 --> 21:27.667
Not at all.

21:27.668 --> 21:30.337
It's because I believed your joke.

21:30.338 --> 21:34.008
But there's no way Iori and Kouhei
could be in that kind of relationship.

21:34.342 --> 21:35.760
Right, you two?

21:38.638 --> 21:39.764
Is that me?

21:41.557 --> 21:43.309
Why aren't you answering?

21:43.518 --> 21:44.893
Could it be you two really...

21:44.894 --> 21:45.685
Is that it?

21:45.686 --> 21:46.978
Absolutely not!

21:46.979 --> 21:48.189
How humiliating!

21:48.564 --> 21:51.859
I guess the strap incident yesterday
made you worry too much.

21:52.151 --> 21:53.319
I'm sorry.

21:53.778 --> 21:55.780
Don't be so tense.

21:57.657 --> 22:01.077
With that attitude, will you be able
to serve customers properly?

22:02.328 --> 22:04.329
It's okay, Chisa.

22:04.330 --> 22:07.124
The boss's way of speaking
is just a bit clumsy.

22:09.961 --> 22:10.545
Yes.

22:19.637 --> 22:21.264
3... 2... 1... Go!

22:30.815 --> 22:33.567
A sweet little love story!?

22:33.568 --> 22:36.319
Asymmetrical reflection in the mirror

22:36.320 --> 22:37.946
A shattered, crunchy heart

22:37.947 --> 22:39.991
Oh oh, stumbling around

22:40.575 --> 22:42.993
Oh oh, just acting on instinct

22:42.994 --> 22:46.955
Diving deep into my subconscious

22:46.956 --> 22:48.707
Tumbling and falling down

22:48.708 --> 22:51.293
A limit-breaking paradise

22:51.294 --> 22:52.544
Viva, cheers

22:52.545 --> 22:54.004
Everyone, cheers

22:54.005 --> 22:56.047
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:56.048 --> 22:56.756
Big trouble

22:56.757 --> 22:58.758
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:58.759 --> 22:59.593
Wa wa wa

22:59.594 --> 23:01.553
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

23:01.554 --> 23:02.262
Wa wa wa wa

23:02.263 --> 23:04.222
Let's go, everybody

23:04.223 --> 23:07.684
Dramatic just like a rainbow

23:07.685 --> 23:10.687
Your troubled smile
is absolutely priceless

23:10.688 --> 23:15.984
Total chaos
getting kissed by an octopus

23:15.985 --> 23:18.737
A mermaid washed up on the shore

23:18.738 --> 23:21.656
Darling drowned down
in the Dragon Palace

23:21.657 --> 23:26.953
The treasure box is just full of alcohol

23:26.954 --> 23:29.664
The ultimate license of our youth

23:29.665 --> 23:32.626
Find the treasure and checkmate

23:32.627 --> 23:37.839
An angel who overslept
from swimming too much

23:37.840 --> 23:39.299
Let's go, everybody

23:39.300 --> 23:40.675
Viva, cheers

23:40.676 --> 23:42.010
Oh yeah

23:42.011 --> 23:43.679
Viva, cheers

23:45.014 --> 23:49.977
NEXT EPISODE: MOTHER
